<!--CLI Documentation — CompileCommand
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.cli.documentation.CompileCommand-->
<clidoc:CompileCommand xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:clidoc="com.machineblocks.bml.cli.documentation"
  xmlns:rdoc="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    machineblocks compile specification
  </is>
  <documentation>
    <![CDATA[
    Syntax:
        machineblocks compile <source-selector> [--source-package <FQN>] [--target-package <FQN>]

        Compiles with target machineblocks-v3-scad. The command does not take a
        target name.
        The selector is one BlockML type selector: an exact block FQN, a package
        selector ending in .*, or a recursive selector ending in .**.
        Resolution is scanTypes from the BlockML framework. This host does not
        define a second selector language.
        Quote tokens that contain * or ** so the shell does not expand them.
        --source-package <FQN> is the source package root for an explicit mapping.
        --target-package <FQN> is the target package root. It is not a directory
        and not the FQN of one output file.
        There is no --out and no --all. The output root is the configured srcDir
        (default blocks).
        A selector only chooses blocks. It does not by itself choose the target
        package, except that a package selector (a final .* or .** segment)
        supplies the source root when --target-package is set and
        --source-package is omitted. An exact block FQN does not supply a source
        root.
        --source-package without --target-package exits 2 with
        MB_SOURCE_PACKAGE_ALONE.
        --target-package without a derivable source root exits 2 with
        MB_SOURCE_PACKAGE_REQUIRED. The message names --source-package.
        A missing selector, an unknown flag, or a selector scanTypes rejects
        exits 2.
        Types whose baseType chain is neither com.machineblocks.bml.core.Block
        nor com.machineblocks.bml.core.Set are skipped. If none remain, the host
        exits 1 with MB_SELECTOR_EMPTY and the selector text.
        Mapping failures, collisions, and paths that leave srcDir or would
        overwrite a .bml file exit 1. No output file is written unless every
        selected block has a target FQN and a legal path, and every compile
        succeeded.
        Exit 0 writes the SCAD or preset JSON files and a sibling .map when the
        target attached a source map, then prints Wrote N file(s) to <srcDir>.
        N counts every written file, including a sibling .map.

        Automatic mapping replaces the one bml segment with scad. An explicit
        mapping swaps sourcePackage for targetPackage and does not apply that
        replacement on top. The path rules and the codes
        MB_TARGET_PACKAGE_UNDETERMINED, MB_TARGET_PACKAGE_AMBIGUOUS, and
        MB_SOURCE_OUTSIDE_ROOT are specified by rdoc:FqnNaming.

        Host diagnostic codes:

        - MB_SOURCE_PACKAGE_ALONE — --source-package without --target-package.
        - MB_SOURCE_PACKAGE_REQUIRED — --target-package and the source root is not
          determined. The message names --source-package.
        - MB_SELECTOR_EMPTY — the selector matched no Block or Set.
        - MB_TARGET_COLLISION — two selected blocks share a target FQN or output path.
        - MB_OUTPUT_ESCAPES_SRC — a resolved path is outside srcDir.
        - MB_OUTPUT_OVERWRITES_BML — a resolved path is an existing .bml file.
        - MB_EMPTY_BLOCK — a composite has nothing to render.

        blockml.config.json srcDir is the output root. mbLibPath defaults to the
        installed @machineblocks/core package. openscadPath is unused by compile.
        A missing mbLibPath and a missing @machineblocks/core install exit 2.

    Printed help:
    Usage: machineblocks compile <source-selector> [--source-package <FQN>] [--target-package <FQN>]
           machineblocks compile --help

    When: render selected Block and Set types to OpenSCAD. Change BML first, then recompile.

    Target is machineblocks-v3-scad. The command does not take a target name.
    The selector is one BlockML type selector: an exact FQN, pkg.*, or pkg.**.
    Quote tokens that contain * or ** so the shell does not expand them.
    Resolution is scanTypes. This host does not define a second selector language.
    Types whose baseType chain is neither com.machineblocks.bml.core.Block nor
    com.machineblocks.bml.core.Set are skipped.

    Output is written under the configured srcDir (default blocks). There is no --out and no --all.
    A package selector (a final .* or .** segment) supplies the source root when
    --target-package is set and --source-package is omitted. An exact block FQN does not.
    Automatic mapping replaces the one bml segment with scad.
    com.example.bml.bricks.MyBrick becomes blocks/com/example/scad/bricks/MyBrick.scad.
    Explicit mapping swaps --source-package for --target-package and does not apply that replacement again.

    Flags:
      --source-package <FQN>   source package root for an explicit mapping
      --target-package <FQN>   target package root. Not a directory and not one output file.

    --source-package without --target-package exits 2 (MB_SOURCE_PACKAGE_ALONE).
    --target-package without a derivable source root exits 2 (MB_SOURCE_PACKAGE_REQUIRED).
    A missing selector, an unknown flag, or a selector scanTypes rejects exits 2.
    If no Block or Set remains, exit 1 (MB_SELECTOR_EMPTY) and the message names the selector.

    Exit 0 writes the SCAD or preset JSON files and a sibling .map when the target attached a source map.
    The status line is Wrote N file(s) to <srcDir>. N counts every written file, including a sibling .map.
    One failure writes nothing. Mapping failures, collisions, and illegal paths exit 1:
      MB_TARGET_COLLISION — two selected blocks share a target FQN or output path.
      MB_OUTPUT_ESCAPES_SRC — a resolved path is outside srcDir.
      MB_OUTPUT_OVERWRITES_BML — a resolved path is an existing .bml file.
      MB_TARGET_PACKAGE_UNDETERMINED — the source FQN has no bml segment.
      MB_TARGET_PACKAGE_AMBIGUOUS — the source FQN has more than one bml segment.
      MB_SOURCE_OUTSIDE_ROOT — a selected block is outside --source-package.
      MB_EMPTY_BLOCK — a composite has nothing to render.

    blockml.config.json srcDir is the output root. mbLibPath defaults to the installed
    @machineblocks/core package. openscadPath is unused by compile.
    A missing mbLibPath and a missing @machineblocks/core install exit 2.

    Related: validate. Search, inspect, graph, and new stay on blockml.
    ]]>
  </documentation>
